            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts announced the case: \u201cWe\u2019ll hear first this morning Case 17\u2011155, Hughes versus the United States.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1cf2255faab-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 9,
              "start": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked: \u201cSo are you conceding there\u2019s no \u2014 you can\u2019t imagine a scenario where someone wouldn\u2019t be eligible?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1cf2255faab-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan asked: \u201cSo, in those circumstances, there is no result?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1cf2255faab-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked: \u201cSuppose that there\u2019s a majority of the Court that agrees a particular party is entitled to relief, but there is no majority as to the provision of the Constitution that provides the relief. What happens in that situation?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1cf2255faab-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 34,
              "start": 34
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked: \u201cWhat guidance?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1cf2255faab-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Gorsuch asked: \u201cNo, I understand you\u2019d like us to decide what we\u2019re calling the Marks question, rather than just resolving what Freeman means.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e1cf2255faab-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 56,
              "start": 56
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor noted the Solicitor General\u2019s statement that when a judge rejects a (C) agreement, the parties return to the starting point, allowing the government to keep its right to file the persistent felony certificate or prosecute dismissed charges."
      }
